    "id": 3517150,
    "postDate": "2026-08-26T09:06:49.657Z",
    "rawMarkdown": "I've tried numerous combinations of LLMs, but the performance consistently plateaus at around 0.89. I suspect this might be the actual capability ceiling for LLMs. Furthermore, in real-world scenarios, different doctors have varying levels of experience and naturally provide different opinions, meaning the ground truth reports themselves aren't absolutely flawless.\n\nBecause of this, I've basically given up on chasing higher metrics. I feel like the ultimate solution might be training multiple models on different labels and relying on trial and error to get better scores. But honestly, this approach feels almost identical to continuous ensembling, which inevitably leads to overfitting.",
    "content": "<p>I've tried numerous combinations of LLMs, but the performance consistently plateaus at around 0.89. I suspect this might be the actual capability ceiling for LLMs. Furthermore, in real-world scenarios, different doctors have varying levels of experience and naturally provide different opinions, meaning the ground truth reports themselves aren't absolutely flawless.</p>\n<p>Because of this, I've basically given up on chasing higher metrics. I feel like the ultimate solution might be training multiple models on different labels and relying on trial and error to get better scores. But honestly, this approach feels almost identical to continuous ensembling, which inevitably leads to overfitting.</p>",
